														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3672104">
									

<p>Well, it's more of a refined delivery vehicle for the &quot;Internet Meme: The Article&quot; concept, so there's that. Can't say that I'm a fan of attempts to do that, but this version of the article is a better attempt at conveying the intended narrative.</p>
<p>The replacement for the interview has traded one set of clunky dialogue for another, however. Now, we've got an unnecessary interview in which John Cena monologues about his nefarious plans, complete with Movie Villain flourish. It shares the same problem as before, in that it's the story being told in the most direct possible manner, in a way that feels very forced by what the story requires, rather than what actual people would say.</p>
<p>I doubt there's a version of this that I'd end up supporting, but this is exhibiting a lot of the same weaknesses as the previous iteration.</p>

							</div>

								
					
